\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Choice of the smoothness weight $\lambda $, shown for Rhône. Each point is one inversion, all sharing the same calibrated dynamical state so that only $\lambda $ varies. (a)~Stronger smoothing lowers the roughness of the profile at the cost of the geometry misfit. (b)~Stake RMSE against $\lambda $; the shaded band marks the range over which the recovered profile is effectively unchanged, and the fit degrades only at the extremes. The star is the adopted $\lambda = 0.05$.}}{10}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:lambda}{{4}{10}{Choice of the smoothness weight $\lambda $, shown for Rhône. Each point is one inversion, all sharing the same calibrated dynamical state so that only $\lambda $ varies. (a)~Stronger smoothing lowers the roughness of the profile at the cost of the geometry misfit. (b)~Stake RMSE against $\lambda $; the shaded band marks the range over which the recovered profile is effectively unchanged, and the fit degrades only at the extremes. The star is the adopted $\lambda = 0.05$}{figure.caption.5}{}}
